        "procedure": "To a suspension of [Nd{N(SiMe3)2}3] (1.40 g, 2.22 mmol) in toluene (60 ml) was added at room temperature a toluene solution (40 ml) of Me3SiOH (0.60 g, 6.66 mmol). After the blue solution had been stirred overnight the solvent was reduced in vacuo to approximately 10 ml. Crystallization at −20 °C gave blue crystals of 1·1/2 C7H8 (0.98 g, 73%) which turned amorphous upon drying in vacuo; mp. 238 °C (dec.).",
